WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:05.850
You cannot talk about a story, without talking
about the underlying moral message that story

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:07.110
is built upon.

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:11.869
This goes for any major piece of literature,
theater or cinematography.

00:00:11.869 --> 00:00:17.869
And One Piece, with its complex web of characters
and ideologies, is no exception to this.

00:00:17.869 --> 00:00:22.630
One of the central moral themes, that is thoroughly
explored in One Piece is justice.

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:26.910
It is a golden thread that spans throughout
the entire story.

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.910
What does it mean to be just?

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:30.359
What rules does it imply?

00:00:30.359 --> 00:00:33.270
And who decides what these rules are?

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:37.780
We explore these questions through the characters
we encounter throughout the story and even

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:43.410
more so through the actions that these characters
then take based on their distinct believes.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:48.829
We follow a main character that despite being
a pirate often acts a lot more justly than

00:00:48.829 --> 00:00:51.739
many of the supposedly good marines.

00:00:51.739 --> 00:00:56.469
And with the revolutionary army, Oda has even
introduced an entity into the story, that

00:00:56.469 --> 00:01:01.590
openly opposes an idea of Justice under which
large parts of the world are suffering.

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:07.120
However, in no other context, is the concept
of justice explored as openly and distinctly

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:10.110
as within the ranks of the marine admirals.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:14.550
Each admiral has a unique perspective and
take on what justice means for them.

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:19.010
And as a consequence, each admiral impacts
the story in very different ways.

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:23.780
In this series, we will take a closer look
at the four marine admirals that we know off

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:29.190
so far and explore together, what their different
ideas of justice truly mean and how they express

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:32.070
themselves in the context of One Piece.

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:36.310
And what better candidate to start with than
the coolest of the four.

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:37.310
Get it?

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:39.080
The coolest?

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:40.250
Never mind.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:45.680
Kuzan, or as he is better known, Aokiji, is
probably the admiral, that we have gotten

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:48.610
the most complete picture off, so far.

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:53.070
Next to his amazing design and his unique
devil fruit power, Aokiji follows the path

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:55.180
of lazy justice.

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:57.930
But how exactly can justice be lazy?

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:00.950
And how does it distinguish him from his fellow
admirals?

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:05.550
If you´ve ever wondered about that: No worries,
that´s why we´re here.

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:09.140
Before we get into the moral structure of
Kuzan´s character though, I first want to

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:12.950
quickly update you guys on our small challenge
we´ve had recently.

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:17.780
Once again, you have beat me to it and reached
the 3000 like mark on the last video a lot

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:19.379
faster than I anticipated.

00:02:19.379 --> 00:02:20.379
Touché.

00:02:20.379 --> 00:02:26.390
So, this time, we´re gonna raise the bar
to 3500 likes in the first 24 hours that this

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:31.640
video is online, and you will get the second
admiral by next Tuesday.

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:35.920
And by the way, if you are wondering why in
the world, I´m trying to get more likes on

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:40.740
these video´s, it´s because, one, it makes
these video´s available to more people and,

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:46.599
two, it motivates me like crazy to work more
consistently to give you guys not only more

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:48.620
but also better content.

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:51.870
So, smash that like button, and make me work.

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:53.629
But enough about that.

00:02:53.629 --> 00:02:57.769
After all we´re here to delve into one of
the most philosophical questions in the entirety

00:02:57.769 --> 00:02:58.769
of storytelling.

00:02:58.769 --> 00:03:05.769
So, let´s take a look at the man who is so
chill that he thinks Justice should be lazy.

00:03:05.769 --> 00:03:12.189
Aokiji, Kuzan is one of the most popular members
of the marines, that most of the time act

00:03:12.189 --> 00:03:14.430
as an antagonistic force to Luffy and his
crew.

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:21.040
He is a tall, slender and muscularly built
man with long, curled black hair and tanned

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:22.040
skin.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:25.920
Despite being the youngest among the admirals
by quite a bit, he nonetheless is without

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:30.409
a doubt one of the strongest characters in
the story, thanks to years of hard training

00:03:30.409 --> 00:03:35.900
as well as his powerful Logia-Devil-Fruit
that turns his entire body into ice.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:40.180
Having joined the ranks of the marines at
a very young age, Aokiji has worked his way

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:42.249
up the ranks fairly quickly.

00:03:42.249 --> 00:03:44.129
Which is no big surprise.

00:03:44.129 --> 00:03:47.790
As we know, he can be very determined and
focused when he needs to.

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:53.599
In general, however, Aokiji is a rather laid-back
person, that enjoys respect and popularity

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:56.129
throughout the ranks of the marines.

00:03:56.129 --> 00:04:01.400
This is most likely not only due to his immense
strength and influence, but also due to his

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:07.549
personality, which is unusually kind and respectful
compared to other high-ranking members.

00:04:07.549 --> 00:04:13.379
As a matter of fact, respect and fairness
are two of the most defining traits for Kuzan´s

00:04:13.379 --> 00:04:14.379
personality.

00:04:14.379 --> 00:04:18.220
Not only does he treat his fellow marines
respectfully and fair, but even acknowledges

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:20.660
alleged criminals for doing good deeds.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:25.510
A great example for this is letting Luffy
and his Crew go free, not only for taking

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:30.870
down the tyrannical Crocodile and liberating
Alabasta, but also out of respect for Luffy´s

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:33.870
will to sacrifice himself for his crew.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:38.100
What makes Aokiji a truly good character in
the eye of the reader, however, is that his

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:43.860
respectfulness and fairness are firmly grounded
in the empathy and compassion he feels for

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:44.860
others.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:48.840
He takes people´s circumstances and their
good intentions into account and wants to

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:52.120
help create a world with less suffering and
pain.

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:56.790
We can see this for instance when he freezes
the entire ocean only to let Tonjit return

00:04:56.790 --> 00:04:59.870
to his clan after the events at the Davy Back
Fight.

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:05.280
But I think nothing proves this point as well
as his relationship with Robin.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:09.990
Even though, he was tasked with tracking her
down and capturing her, he was genuinely relieved

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:13.480
and happy that she had finally found true
friends.

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:18.050
All of that, despite the straw hats just invading
invaded Ennis Lobby and having declared war

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:20.720
against the world government itself.

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:26.940
Aokiji however is aware of Robin´s true personality
and how she had no fault at becoming a criminal

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:28.770
in the eyes of the world.

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:33.160
Which is exactly why he allowed her to flee
the slaughter on her Island many years ago

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:35.280
in the first place.

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:40.550
You may ask yourself now, how someone this
caring and apparently soft could possibly

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:44.840
become an admiral in the otherwise so hard-boiled
marines.

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:49.100
As a matter of fact, many of the marines asked
themselves the same question.

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:52.030
But the answer to that is quite simple.

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:56.150
Kuzan has an incredibly strong sense of duty.

00:05:56.150 --> 00:06:00.160
Even though he allows himself to live according
to his morals most of the time, when it is

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:04.830
expected of him, he is always ready to follow
orders and do what is expected of him as an

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:06.050
admiral.

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:10.360
During the war at Marineford for example,
he grudgingly drops his usual laid-back and

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:14.400
friendly nature and trades it for a more ruthless
and unforgiving personality.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:20.640
And when encountering Robin and the straw
hats for the first time, he at first decides

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:26.290
to leave them alone, before changing his mind
and trying to take Robin, only to flip-flop

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:28.820
again after seeing Luffy stand up for her.

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:33.760
What becomes painfully clear, when we look
at this example, is how conflicted Aokiji

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:38.720
is between his own idea of how to act morally
and his duty as a member of the marines and

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:39.720
the world government.

00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:46.350
As you might have suspected, all of this also
plays a decisive role in his sense of justice.

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:52.740
So now, in order to understand what lazy justice
actually means, let´s have a look at Aokiji´s

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:56.080
character arc.

00:06:56.080 --> 00:07:01.770
To understand what Kuzan means, when he talks
about his lazy justice, we first have to understand

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:05.800
how his character has developed over the course
of the story.

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:11.120
Despite the admirals not getting a lot of
screen time in the story, Aokiji has nonetheless

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:14.210
undergone a significant change of perspective.

00:07:14.210 --> 00:07:18.720
As a base for that, we have to look at the
admiral in his younger days, where he was

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:20.790
still a vice-admiral.

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:25.270
To be more precise even, we have to look at
the events surrounding the destruction of

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:27.510
the island of Ohara.

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:32.280
Back in time Aokiji had a very different take
on justice in general.

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:36.480
When first informed about the events on the
island by his men, he doesn´t really care

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:38.490
about the fate of the Island.

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:44.340
For him it is simply the fate of criminals,
that have to be taken out to protect the peace.

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:49.870
He only changes his mind, when he learns that
his friend Jaguar D. Saul, who previously

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:54.970
had deserted the marines to save Robin´s
mother Olivia, is also on Ohara.

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:59.490
When arriving on the island, he appears indifferent
to the injustice that is happening there in

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:01.210
the name of the world government.

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:06.500
And at first Kuzan decides to follow his sense
of duty and takes down his old friend Saul

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:09.710
himself, who is trying to escape with Robin.

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:15.050
When Saul confronts him about the massacre
going on, Aokiji says that he has no opinion

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:16.360
about it.

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:22.710
But we can already read from this response,
that he is not at all happy with what is happening.

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:28.450
Just a short time later however he has to
witness Akainu sinking a ship full of refugees,

00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:32.700
simply on the whim that some of the scholars
might have sneaked on board.

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:36.050
This seems to be THE decisive turning point
for him.

00:08:36.050 --> 00:08:40.680
It becomes very clear that Aokiji indeed DID
have an opinion about what was happening,

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:44.740
and he decides to let the innocent girl Robin
escape the island.

00:08:44.740 --> 00:08:49.850
What this shows us, is that Aokiji has always
been good at heart, but forcefully has put

00:08:49.850 --> 00:08:52.339
his duty before his own ideals.

00:08:52.339 --> 00:08:56.480
He needed to realize the brutal lengths to
which the world government would go to protect

00:08:56.480 --> 00:08:57.740
its power.

00:08:57.740 --> 00:09:01.870
And he also needed to learn how to put his
own morality into his actions as well and

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:05.060
distance himself from the justice practiced
by the higher ups.

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:10.209
That is what the incident of Ohara was all
about for his character.

00:09:10.209 --> 00:09:15.110
So now we know how Aokiji got to follow his
path of lazy justice.

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:21.029
But we still don´t quite know what lazy is
actually supposed to mean in this context.

00:09:21.029 --> 00:09:26.920
As a matter of fact, lazy can be seen in quite
a variety of ways when it comes to justice.

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:32.430
I would argue that Aokiji labels his justice
as lazy to distinguish himself from his fellow

00:09:32.430 --> 00:09:33.800
admiral Akainu.

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:39.350
While Akainu´s absolute justice leaves no
room for interpretation and situation-based

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:44.870
morality, Kuzan´s justice is lazy in the
sense that it is not always necessary to take

00:09:44.870 --> 00:09:47.200
action no matter what.

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:52.300
Sometimes it might be the right thing to take
a look at things first and see how they develop.

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:55.550
This is exactly what we see him doing most
of the time.

00:09:55.550 --> 00:10:01.370
Observing but not taking action, unless he
sees a truly justifiable reason for it.

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:05.980
But even more so than that, I would argue
that with the phrase lazy, Aokiji is actually

00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:08.620
hiding his true idea of justice.

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:11.350
Which is moral justice.

00:10:11.350 --> 00:10:16.101
When we strip away all the distractions around
his character, at his core, Aokiji´s idea

00:10:16.101 --> 00:10:18.329
of justice is based on his values.

00:10:18.329 --> 00:10:23.129
In other words: Compassion, respect and fairness.

00:10:23.129 --> 00:10:27.680
Since this very liberal take on the issue
conflicts heavily with that of the world government

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:33.560
however, Kuzan can use his laziness as an
excuse to actually take moral action in critical

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:35.079
situations.

00:10:35.079 --> 00:10:39.441
While most people will see it as him being
lazy and undetermined, Aokiji actually is

00:10:39.441 --> 00:10:42.720
able to make himself a clear image of a situation.

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:47.970
He can assess whether someone deserves respect
or compassion and what the fair and right

00:10:47.970 --> 00:10:49.649
thing to do is.

00:10:49.649 --> 00:10:53.700
This allows him to let Robin go on Ohara,
letting the straw hats get away after the

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:59.100
Davie Back Fight or letting Luffy of the hook
several times during Marineford, not dealing

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:02.809
the fatal blow or chasing after Laws submarine.

00:11:02.809 --> 00:11:06.970
And even when he tries to uphold his sense
of duty toward the marines, we can always

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:11.050
see glints of mercy and understanding in his
actions.

00:11:11.050 --> 00:11:16.069
Even though it is quite unique in the ranks
of the Marines, Kuzan believes in second chances

00:11:16.069 --> 00:11:19.509
and he usually gives people the benefit of
doubt.

00:11:19.509 --> 00:11:23.430
Seeing how he actually cares for Robin and
feels responsible for what happened to her

00:11:23.430 --> 00:11:28.309
in the past, really shows us how different
Aokiji is from his superiors.

00:11:28.309 --> 00:11:32.949
Which is exactly why I believe that in the
end he went his own way.

00:11:32.949 --> 00:11:38.730
After having to kill his close friend on Ohara
and swallow his morality during the war, Kuzan

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:40.070
decided to change something.

00:11:40.070 --> 00:11:45.470
He tried to turn the marines into a more compassionate
and positive organization that works for the

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:50.649
people after being suggested as the new fleet
admiral by Sengoku himself.

00:11:50.649 --> 00:11:56.559
Being defeated by Akainu however, he saw no
purpose in continuing his work as an admiral.

00:11:56.559 --> 00:12:03.119
Instead, he now is free to act based on his
own idea of justice, freed from any restriction

00:12:03.119 --> 00:12:04.569
or doubt.

00:12:04.569 --> 00:12:08.959
Now the question here of course is, whether
Aokiji is actually still a marine at heart

00:12:08.959 --> 00:12:10.579
or not.

00:12:10.579 --> 00:12:15.390
Currently he seems to be affiliated with the
Blackbeard Pirates in some shape or form.

00:12:15.390 --> 00:12:21.300
However, after being saved by him from Doflamingo,
Smoker asks Aokiji who he now is.

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:26.899
But the former admiral reassures his friend
that as a matter of fact he is still himself.

00:12:26.899 --> 00:12:30.660
Well, does he mean by that that he is still
a marine?

00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:31.690
Possibly.

00:12:31.690 --> 00:12:36.720
But most importantly, I think that Aokiji
is still himself in the sense that he is a

00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:39.180
man of his own justice.

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:43.399
Someone who now is able to follow his own
path of moral justice.

00:12:43.399 --> 00:12:47.269
And it´s okay if to others it looks like
it is lazy.

00:12:47.269 --> 00:12:50.890
After all, Aokiji is a pretty cool dude.

00:12:50.890 --> 00:12:53.860
